# Game / Identifier Variables
gid – [object/int64] unique game identifier (often includes team + date encoding).
 id – [object/int64] player or event identifier depending on dataset context.
 team – [object] team abbreviation for the player/event.
 opp – [object] opposing team abbreviation.
 date – [int64] game date in YYYYMMDD format.
 number – [int64] game number within the season or series.
 site – [object] ballpark or stadium code where the game was played.
 vishome – [object] indicates whether a team is visiting (v) or home (h).
 gametype – [object] type of game (e.g., regular season, postseason).
# Batting Order / Role Variables
b_lp – [int64] lineup position or batting position appearance count.
 b_seq – [int64] sequence of plate appearances in game.
 dh – [int64] designated hitter indicator (1 = yes, 0 = no).
 ph – [int64] pinch hitter indicator.
 pr – [int64] pinch runner indicator.
# Plate Appearance / Batting Outcome Stats
b_pa – [int64] plate appearances.
 b_ab – [int64] at-bats.
 b_r – [int64] runs scored.
 b_h – [int64] hits.
 b_d – [int64] doubles.
 b_t – [int64] triples.
 b_hr – [int64] home runs.
 b_rbi – [int64] runs batted in.
 b_sh – [int64] sacrifice hits (bunts).
 b_sf – [int64] sacrifice flies.
 b_hbp – [int64] hit by pitch.
 b_w – [int64] walks (bases on balls).
 b_iw – [int64] intentional walks.
 b_k – [int64] strikeouts.
 b_sb – [int64] stolen bases.
 b_cs – [int64] caught stealing.
 b_gdp – [int64] grounded into double play.
 b_xi – [int64] reached base on interference or similar scoring event.
 b_roe – [int64] reached on error.
# Game Outcome / Context Variables
win – [int64] indicator if player’s team won (1 = win, 0 = no).
 loss – [int64] indicator if team lost.
 tie – [int64] indicator of tie game (rare in MLB modern data).
 box – [object/int64] box score availability or identifier flag.
 pbp – [object/int64] play-by-play data availability or identifier flag.
 eject – [int64] whether player was ejected (1 = yes, 0 = no).
 value – [float64] computed performance or contribution metric (dataset-specific scoring value).
# Team / Game Encoding Variables
BOS194108061 – [object] encoded game ID (team + date format example).
 sturj101 – [object] player ID (MLBAM-style identifier).
 NYA – [object] team abbreviation (example instance).
 ARI201208110 – [object] encoded game ID (Arizona game example).
 wheer001 – [object] player ID (MLBAM-style identifier).
# League / Division / Standings Variables
division_id – [int64] identifier for division.
 year – [int64] season year.
 games – [int64] total games played (team or player-season level depending on aggregation).
 ab – [int64] at-bats (season-level aggregate).
 hits – [int64] total hits (season-level).
 hr – [int64] home runs (season-level).
 doubles – [int64] doubles.
 triples – [int64] triples.
 rbi – [int64] runs batted in.
 walks – [int64] walks.
 k – [int64] strikeouts.
 sb – [int64] stolen bases.
 avg – [float64] batting average.
# Awards / Season Outcomes
home_games – [int64] number of home games played.
 division_winner – [int64] indicator if team won division.
 wild_card_winner – [int64] indicator if team won wild card.
 league_winner – [int64] indicator if team won league championship.
 world_series_winner – [int64] indicator if team won World Series.
# Aggregate League Statistics (Context Variables)
strikeouts_by_batters – [int64] total strikeouts by batters in dataset scope.
 stolen_bases – [int64] total stolen bases.
 caught_stealing – [int64] total caught stealing.
 batters_hit_by_pitch – [int64] total HBP events.
 sacrifice_flies – [int64] total sacrifice flies.
 home_attendance – [int64] attendance at home games.
